  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting respect of rights of LGBTI older adults in Costa Rica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIPAC, working with older adult volunteers and other organizations across the country, will validate a newly developed training guide and materials, conduct Training-of- Trainers (TOT) activities, and conduct various workshops on improving awareness of the needs of older LGBTI adults in Costa Rica. It will also develop and implement an advocacy plan to put the specific needs of older LGBTI adults on the agendas of community groups that work with this population. This project will directly benefit approximately 290 people and at least 1,000 LGBTI Costa Ricans will benefit indirectly through improved understanding of older adult sexual orientation and needs.</narrative>
  </description>
